course: dictionary
lesson: 4658
title: The strange hoatzin
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can learn a lot about a new word from the words around it. «Young hoatzins have claws on their wings, so after dropping into the water to escape a snake they swim and climb back up to the nest.» The clues are claws on their wings, climb back up and nest, so a hoatzin is a bird that uses its wings to climb.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here? The sentence is about a bird that falls into water and needs to get back to its nest in a tree. Try the meaning in the sentence: "Young birds have claws on their wings, so after dropping into the water they climb back up to the nest." It still makes sense, so you have understood it.
explain: A hoatzin is a real bird, and a dictionary can tell you more. It lives in the Amazon rainforest in South America. It has a spiky crest, a blue face and red eyes. It eats leaves and smells bad, so it is also called the stinkbird.
fact: A hoatzin is a strange bird of the Amazon rainforest in South America.
fact: A hoatzin has a spiky crest, a blue face and red eyes.
fact: Hoatzins eat leaves and smell bad, so they are also called stinkbirds.
fact: Young hoatzins have claws on their wings to help them climb back into trees.
fact: The hoatzin is the national bird of Guyana.
exercise: «Young hoatzins have claws on their wings, so after dropping into the water to escape a snake they swim and climb back up to the nest.» Why do young hoatzins have claws on their wings? | *To climb back up into trees after dropping into water | To hold on to snakes | To fly faster than other birds | To dig holes in the ground
exercise: Where does the hoatzin live? | *In the Amazon rainforest in South America | In the Scottish hills | On a London rooftop | In the Australian desert
exercise: A hoatzin is also called a stinkbird. What clue tells you why? | *It eats leaves and smells bad | It lives only in the sea | It sings loudly at night | It has a long, bright tail
test: What colour is the hoatzin's face? | *Blue | Green | Yellow | Black
test: What does the hoatzin eat? | Fish | Insects | *Leaves | Seeds
exam: Which country has the hoatzin as its national bird? | Peru | *Guyana | Brazil | Australia
